# DNA-AND content · minerals and what each kind of ground is made of
# researched: standard mineralogy (mineral formulas as in mineral reference tables); crust make-up from geology
#   references (Earth's continental crust is mostly feldspars and quartz, with pyroxene, clays, micas, calcite and
#   iron oxides; basalt is mostly pyroxene, calcic plagioclase and olivine; the Moon's highlands are anorthite-rich,
#   its seas basalt with ilmenite; Mars's dust is basalt minerals reddened by hematite; icy worlds are water ice with
#   frozen carbon dioxide, nitrogen and methane). Shares are rough parts per 100 of the grains.
# Each grain of ground is one mineral, picked from its ground's mix; zooming into it shows that mineral's own atoms.
# grain-mm: the grains' sizes across, smallest to largest (Wentworth scale: sand 0.0625 to 2 mm, silt 0.0039 to 0.0625 mm,
#   clay below 0.0039 mm; dune sand mostly 0.2 to 0.5 mm; the Moon's dust about 0.04 to 0.1 mm; snow grains 0.1 to 2 mm).
# Crystal faces step down in single layers about 0.2 to 0.3 nm high, with flat terraces between usually 10 to 100 nm wide.
# atoms: the formula's atoms written out one by one (its real ratio); colour: the grain's colour as seen (0 to 1).
# lustre: how its surface takes light (mineral reference tables: vitreous like glass, metallic, pearly, resinous, waxy,
#   earthy (dull), wet); clarity: clear, translucent or opaque. Every grain, stone and thing is drawn by these, never by name.
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · content/elements.dnat · content/geology.dnat

@mineral quartz
name: Quartz
formula: SiO2
atoms: Si O O
colour: 0.86 0.82 0.74
lustre: vitreous
clarity: clear

@mineral albite
name: Albite (sodium feldspar)
formula: NaAlSi3O8
atoms: Na Al Si Si Si O O O O O O O O
colour: 0.9 0.88 0.84
lustre: vitreous
clarity: translucent

@mineral orthoclase
name: Orthoclase (potassium feldspar)
formula: KAlSi3O8
atoms: K Al Si Si Si O O O O O O O O
colour: 0.88 0.7 0.62
lustre: vitreous
clarity: translucent

@mineral anorthite
name: Anorthite (calcium feldspar)
formula: CaAl2Si2O8
atoms: Ca Al Al Si Si O O O O O O O O
colour: 0.82 0.82 0.8
lustre: vitreous
clarity: translucent

@mineral forsterite
name: Olivine (forsterite)
formula: Mg2SiO4
atoms: Mg Mg Si O O O O
colour: 0.55 0.66 0.3
lustre: vitreous
clarity: translucent

@mineral fayalite
name: Olivine (fayalite)
formula: Fe2SiO4
atoms: Fe Fe Si O O O O
colour: 0.42 0.38 0.2
lustre: vitreous
clarity: translucent

@mineral enstatite
name: Pyroxene (enstatite)
formula: MgSiO3
atoms: Mg Si O O O
colour: 0.4 0.38 0.3
lustre: vitreous
clarity: translucent

@mineral augite
name: Pyroxene (augite)
formula: CaMgSi2O6
atoms: Ca Mg Si Si O O O O O O
colour: 0.22 0.22 0.2
lustre: vitreous
clarity: opaque

@mineral kaolinite
name: Clay (kaolinite)
formula: Al2Si2O5(OH)4
atoms: Al Al Si Si O O O O O O O O O H H H H
colour: 0.84 0.78 0.66
lustre: earthy
clarity: opaque

@mineral biotite
name: Mica (biotite)
formula: KMg3AlSi3O10(OH)2
atoms: K Mg Mg Mg Al Si Si Si O O O O O O O O O O O O H H
colour: 0.25 0.2 0.14
lustre: pearly
clarity: translucent

@mineral calcite
name: Calcite
formula: CaCO3
atoms: Ca C O O O
colour: 0.94 0.92 0.86
lustre: vitreous
clarity: clear

@mineral hematite
name: Hematite
formula: Fe2O3
