lustre: vitreous
clarity: clear

@mineral methane-ice
name: Methane ice
formula: CH4
atoms: C H H H H
colour: 0.82 0.74 0.66
lustre: waxy
clarity: translucent

# ── what each kind of ground is made of: mineral share, mineral share, ... (parts per 100) ──

@mix temperate
name: Land of a temperate world
grain-mm: 0.1..0.5
minerals: quartz 25, albite 18, orthoclase 14, kaolinite 12, augite 6, biotite 5, calcite 8, hematite 5, magnetite 3, forsterite 2, gypsum 2

@mix desert
name: Dry rocky ground
grain-mm: 0.2..0.5
minerals: quartz 22, hematite 14, albite 14, augite 14, forsterite 10, enstatite 6, magnetite 6, gypsum 6, halite 4, calcite 4

@mix lava
name: Fresh basalt and lava rock
grain-mm: 0.2..1
minerals: augite 28, anorthite 26, forsterite 18, fayalite 6, magnetite 10, ilmenite 6, sulfur 4, pyrite 2

@mix snowball
name: Frozen ground
grain-mm: 0.2..1
minerals: water-ice 70, dry-ice 10, nitrogen-ice 5, methane-ice 5, forsterite 5, enstatite 5

@mix moon
name: Moon ground
grain-mm: 0.04..0.1
minerals: anorthite 40, augite 22, forsterite 14, ilmenite 14, fayalite 5, quartz 5

@mix tidally-locked
name: Ground of a tidally locked world
grain-mm: 0.1..0.5
minerals: augite 22, anorthite 18, quartz 14, hematite 14, forsterite 12, water-ice 10, magnetite 10

@mix ocean
name: Sea floor
grain-mm: 0.01..0.06
minerals: augite 30, anorthite 25, forsterite 15, calcite 15, kaolinite 10, pyrite 5

@mix sea
name: The sea
grain-mm: 0..0
minerals: sea-water 100

@mix ice
name: Sea ice and ice sheets
grain-mm: 0.2..1
minerals: water-ice 100

# ── what lies on a grain's surface, everywhere, at its real size (soil science: clay platelets 0.2 to 2 um across,
#   iron-oxide coatings 0.1 to 1 um, iron-oxide nanoparticles 5 to 50 nm, and a film of water one or two molecules thick
#   from the air on every mineral surface). size-km: smallest to largest across; chance: how many of its cells hold one
#   (a cell is 4 of its largest size); mineral: what it is made of (you go into its own atoms); shape: flat (a plate or a
#   skin), round, or molecule (drawn atom by atom from its mineral, with its bond length in nm and bond angle in degrees).
@surface clay-platelet
name: A clay platelet (kaolinite)
mineral: kaolinite
size-km: 2e-10 2e-9
chance: 0.6
shape: flat
about: a thin six-sided plate, Al2Si2O5(OH)4 | left by water slowly weathering feldspar

@surface iron-coating
name: An iron-oxide coating
mineral: hematite
size-km: 1e-10 1e-9
chance: 0.5
shape: flat
about: a skin of iron oxide (hematite, goethite) | it colours sand red, orange and yellow

@surface nanoparticle
name: An iron-oxide nanoparticle
mineral: hematite
size-km: 5e-12 5e-11
chance: 0.5
shape: round
about: a speck of hematite or goethite, Fe2O3 / FeOOH | a few thousand atoms of iron and oxygen

@surface water
name: A water molecule of the surface film
mineral: water-ice
size-km: 2.8e-13 3.2e-13
chance: 0.6
shape: molecule
bond-nm: 0.0957
angle: 104.5
about: H2O, bent at 104.5 degrees | from the air: every mineral surface wears a film | one or two molecules thick
